// Article 2. Holidays.
#require "1-schedule.charter".
Fact holiday Identified by Winter, Spring
Function holiday-parent Identified by holiday * parent
Fact in-progress Identified by holiday
Event holiday-begins Related to holiday Creates in-progress(holiday)
Bool resuming
Event holiday-ends Related to holiday
  Terminates in-progress(holiday)
  Creates resuming() For 1
Duty holiday-time Holder other Claimant parent
  Holds when parent != other && (Exists holiday: in-progress(holiday) && holiday-parent(holiday, parent))
  Violated when with(other) && Held(holiday-time()) For 1
Extend Duty regular-week
  Overridden by holiday-time
  Conditioned by Not(resuming())

Clause 2.1 Approved "baa64b56b7ad4fef3b1ff0ddcd815cbf8432432912888ae81fa44432aabd5ac1"
  Definition "Mia spends the winter holiday with Daniel and the spring holiday with Rosa."
Clause 2.2 Approved "94f4e07f4d87053924fe31c959e39bf29a0cb4dc405765d4c974fe7e178fd8ec"
  Norm "The holiday schedule overrides the regular schedule. While a holiday lasts, the parent who has the holiday keeps Mia even in the other parent's week." => holiday-time, regular-week
.
+holiday-parent(Winter, Daniel). +holiday-parent(Spring, Rosa).
